WEBVTT

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.030
<b>Episode 18: Amamiya Yuuhi and Shinonome Hangetsu</b>

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.950
The princess is bedridden after 
turning Loki into Hresvelgr.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.610
Akane-kun did a great job discovering 
and defeating the final golem.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.980
Yeah.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.330
And now we have all three 
Mythic Beast Knights.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.860
That's true.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.040
By the way, why did you call us here today?

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.050
Actually, I'm having trouble 
with ideas for my golems.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.400
You're in a slump?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.630
Yeah.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.370
So I decided to ask the opinions 
of our thinker, Amamiya,

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.960
our warrior, Hakudou,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.970
and our expert on psychics, Anima.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.480
He's speaking to you.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.940
How have you made them so far?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.910
I already had a rough idea of shape in mind.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.430
Then I felt like I could do it,

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.780
and from there I just followed 
the flow of my power.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.440
I doubt we'll be getting 
proper input from Anima.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.740
She's just here to eat.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.860
The Creation Field: Kybele.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.460
It's so unique that it's hard 
to give an opinion.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.940
Why don't we try drawing ideas on this?

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.130
That's it!

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.050
What do you think?

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.390
Hands are heads

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.390
You suck.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.460
Wow!

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.100
Nagumocchi, that's amazing!

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:26.940
Well?

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.410
I-It's good!

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.390
It looks strong!

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:30.900
It's a ship!

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.150
Lend me that.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.140
You signed your name to someone else's art?!

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.870
What a fiend!

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.870
This has been good stimulation.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.010
I'll gladly use your art as references.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.860
Anima, why don't you offer 
at least a word of advice?

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:51.460
Hmm?

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.900
The foundation of all 
superpowers is conviction.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.620
You have to have conviction 
deep in your subconscious

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.050
that the phenomenon will happen.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.780
If you're lost, then listen to your gut.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.090
If you can't hear your gut,

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.350
then know that you're just 
plugging your own ears.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.300
Plugging my own ears?

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.420
It's unusual for you to ask others for help.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.450
Honestly asking others for help 
is the first step towards happiness.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.690
Hey.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.530
<i>When I looked up, 
that sky was full of wonders.</i>

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:48.830
<i>The despair I bottled up tormented me,</i>

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:52.800
<i>and I wanted the courage 
to break my chains of isolation.</i>

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.070
<i>(You are my light)</i>

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:59.660
<i>I was searching for your 
brilliant light in my hazy dreams</i>

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.960
<i>to kick away the limits placed on myself.</i>

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.920
<i>Now with your courage, 
let's soar into the sky.</i>

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.630
<i>Let's CRUSH the fear!</i>

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:16.770
<i>I swear to you, at the ends 
of this chaotic world,</i>

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.380
<i>that even if you fall, I'll</i>

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.740
<i>Be the HERO!</i>

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.920
<i>I'll be waiting at the future 
we're moving toward,</i>

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.870
<i>with a “YES, MY LORD!” 
for your constant radiance,</i>

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.880
<i>clutching the stars raining down upon us.</i>

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:42.620
<i>I'll love you until we reach 
that future you want to destroy.</i>

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.380
Animus, did you need something?

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.350
Maimakterion had something 
he wanted to say to you.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.930
This one did?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.120
The Knights are fast, 
so my attacks won't hit,

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.400
but a single blow would kill them if it did

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.390
So fighting them is boring.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.230
I'm getting a little irritated.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:22.780
Your slow blockheads are the only ones 
that will take my attacks.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.070
So produce one that's even sturdier.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.620
Not that shallow junk that just looks strong.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.500
I want to fight more!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:42.220
Apparently, his emotions have grown 
stronger after experiencing battle.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.850
Though I'd prefer not to 
fight you if possible.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.890
How about it?

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.870
This might be your last chance.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.520
Would you like to join me?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.890
I'm opposed.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.520
Be quiet.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.900
You can't surpass my golems.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:00.860
I'm not so sure.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:05.090
You can't because your power 
is an imitation of mine.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.260
That's your limit as a human.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.820
You're a human, too.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.300
I'm a god.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.290
I have no limits.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.310
Then I'll defeat you and become 
the new main character of this myth.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.820
So, no deal?

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.130
Looks like it.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.130
Tch.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:24.810
I'll be waiting in the mountains.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.400
Hey.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.760
Shimaki.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.270
Please watch over this child 
for a little longer.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.140
Loki, stop.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:43.020
I plan on waiting until the final battle 
to see what answer Akane-kun arrives at.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.240
Ah, there you are!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.340
Akane-kun!

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.060
Are you three heading somewhere together?

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.660
Yeah, to the ramen shop!

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.040
Wow, what a face!

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:55.490
I'm sorry.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.500
Did I hit you that hard back then?

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:01.710
This is, um... from the tenth.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.720
Your face is red. Do you have a cold?

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.420
I-I'm fine.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.150
Are you sure you're okay?

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.700
I'm fine.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.930
If you can't hear your gut,

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.020
then know that you're just 
plugging your own ears.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.940
...that shallow junk that just looks strong.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.820
That's your limit...

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:26.600
This isn't like you.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.840
You usually do incredible 
things like it's nothing.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.990
You're full of confidence, 
and you never waver.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.080
Yeah.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:36.300
I was confident in how well
Freitag turned out.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.620
Perhaps that's why.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.420
Though, true.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.460
I am confident.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.270
And people like me don't 
set limits on themselves.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:49.630
I'll try to hear that voice of conviction 
even through the hands covering my ears.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.630
Thanks, Kuh.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.660
I'll do my best.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:04.900
This is Sonnabend.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.130
Huh? Isn't that the one you drew?

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:11.110
Yeah, this is impressive! I'm moved!

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.020
Yeah! Let me fight it!

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.200
Um, I'd like to, too.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.910
That's what I called all of you here for.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.320
It looks quite intense.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.880
Doesn't seem suited 
to practice battles, though.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:26.240
Mikazuki-kun is fast,

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:28.740
and Hakudou-san's a Mythic Beast 
Knight, so they should be fine.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.030
All right, miss, let's do this!

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.720
Yes, let's.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.450
It looks strong.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.820
I'll go all out from the start!

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:42.390
Invincible!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:45.850
Holding Field: Myriad Headed Orochi!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.290
You made him cry.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.790
It's all right, Hakudou-san.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:08.190
I'm glad I didn't use one that weak 
in a real battle against the eleventh.

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.380
So please, don't worry about it.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:22.140
Amamiya-kun, you said you had 
a good change of pace for me?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.460
Yes, digging holes.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:27.610
Nothing beats exercise 
for stimulating the brain.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:33.180
Plus, digging holes is an advanced 
fusion of wisdom and instinct

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:36.660
that ancient mankind developed 
to secure both shelter and safety,

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.820
so it's extremely...

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.440
Anyway,

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.670
to put it simply, it's fun.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:48.040
Eventually you stop feeling the fatigue 
and gain a sense of elation.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.130
You get that "runner's high".

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:55.330
Then, eventually, I stop being able to tell 
if I'm the shovel or if the shovel is me,

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:59.650
and when I step back 
and I realize that I'm human,

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:03.180
that moment of relief is the best 
stimulation for the brain.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.960
He's crazy.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.190
Though he's built up incredible stamina 
ever since that became his new hobby.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.620
You're more physically-minded 
than I thought.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.700
You think so?

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.530
I think it's an extremely 
intellectual activity.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.000
Well, guess I'll give it a try.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.650
You can lose yourself in it.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.020
Phew.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.880
Still, I never knew this before.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.480
Knew what?

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.480
Well, you invited me out 
for a change of pace,

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.090
got us all covered in dirt, and so on.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:41.430
I always thought you were 
more of an introvert.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:44.060
You're kind of incredible, Amamiya-kun.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:46.390
I'm not incredible.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.560
You think so?

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.940
You've changed. Or perhaps,

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:56.970
this is what your original 
personality was like, Yuuhi.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.190
Who knows?

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.540
So good.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.040
Family

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.020
Hello?

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.850
<i>U-Um, listen, Yuu-kun, 
stay, stay calm and listen.</i>

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.940
Auntie, please calm down.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.270
<i>Your grandfather—</i>

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:17.500
Huh?

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.750
My grandpa?

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.110
A truck?

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:25.980
<i>My grandpa died.</i>

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.070
<i>Apparently it was a traffic accident.</i>

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.470
<i>His death was caused by bad luck.</i>

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:34.160
Well, I guess that's life.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:38.860
What?

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.080
There aren't words for it!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.630
Your grandfather...

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:46.200
We healed him with the wish from your pact,

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.710
so this is so unreasonable! 
For him to die like this...

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.040
Every person dies someday.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.860
If death is unreasonable, then so is life.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.490
Playing with words now?!

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.130
Let's have some tea together.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.630
Yuu-nii, you've changed.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.500
It's like you've mellowed out.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.560
Have I?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.850
You have.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.310
Hey, want to head out somewhere?

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:19.180
Grandpa often came to this 
postbox to mail you letters.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:20.130
Letters?

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.400
But I never got one.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.990
He always came home without sending them.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.450
Here, the letters he never sent.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.870
Amamiya Yuuhi-sama

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.450
There's a lot of them.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:31.120
Yuu-nii.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:31.830
Yeah?

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.180
Even though Grandpa's gone, 
come home sometimes, okay?

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:40.640
<i>The letters contained 
standard seasonal greetings,</i>

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.840
<i>questions about what I was eating, 
how my studies went,</i>

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:46.490
<i>reporting that Koishi 
got top marks on her test,</i>

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:48.350
<i>all those kinds of silly little things.</i>

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:52.330
<i>He wrote them every month 
and never sent any of them.</i>

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.830
<i>But the last line of each letter 
was always the same.</i>

00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:59.780
<i>Yuuhi, when are you coming home again?</i>

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:01.740
Well, at the very least,

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.190
I didn't feel like coming home at that time.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.650
Don't make enemies! 
They'll stab you in your gut!

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:22.560
Don't make friends! 
They'll stab you in your back!

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.800
People are all scumbags!

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:30.470
You damn old fart!

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:34.270
People aren't scumbags!

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.400
Serves you right!

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:41.310
Yuuhi...

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:43.590
Have you forgiven your grandfather?

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.460
Well, he is dead and all now.

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:50.770
The truly great are those who can forgive.

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:57.100
Yuuhi.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.900
Mm? Grandpa?

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.430
Yuuhi, do you have a moment?

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.930
Is there anything you want to ask me?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.670
I heard you ignored the traffic signal?

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:12.920
Usually there's hardly any traffic there, 
so I wasn't paying attention.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:15.390
I feel bad for the driver.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.400
Oh, so there wasn't any real reason for it?

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:24.360
Yeah. Looks I died for no particular reason.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.810
Were there any last words 
you wanted to leave behind?

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:29.410
Yeah.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:31.910
Welcome home.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.070
Yeah.

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:35.240
I'm home.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.490
Dad, shall we get going?

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:41.000
Yeah, I'm on my way now.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:43.850
Take it easy.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.260
Farewell, Grandpa.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.090
Was that a dream?

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.030
Or did he actually come to visit me?

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.720
It's all subjective.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.580
Believe whatever you'd like to believe.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:11.150
Then I will.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.370
Yuu-kun, an order for you.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:15.940
Come here.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:20.790
Amamiya Yuuhi.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:25.630
Normally you come here 
at Samidare's sole invitation,

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.820
so only the aggressive portion of your mind

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:31.300
that sympathizes with Earth's 
destruction manifested here,

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.220
but this time I have invited you, as well,

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:37.770
so your full consciousness 
and personality are here.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:43.780
So you'll remember everything you're about 
to experience here when you awaken.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.360
Are you going to make me do something?

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:49.470
Once you overcome the trial I'm about 
to give you, I'll give you a hint.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.320
Take that information back with you.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.520
Trial?

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.740
All three Mythic Beast Knights are together,

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:57.810
you've destroyed one of Animus' 
three Celestial Bodies,

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:00.290
and you, the key, 
have undergone your purification.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.330
The key?

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:04.090
This tale is in its final chapters.

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:06.050
<b>To Amamiya Yuuhi</b>

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:06.630
<b>Anima is
betting on you.</b>

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:09.260
Why... me?

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.460
Go on, now.

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:14.260
Yes.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.850
I expect great things from you, my Knight.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.630
Leave it to me, my Lucifer.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.210
I had a dream the other day.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.630
You were racing up 
a long flight of stairs...

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.810
Shinonome-san.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.270
Hey, Yuu-kun.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.290
Odd place for us to meet.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:04.120
That's true. Although...

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.980
I had a feeling you would be here.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.200
Yeah.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.720
So I don't really know what's going on,

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:13.520
but, apparently, I'm supposed to stop 
anyone from climbing these stairs.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:14.450
Yeah.

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:15.930
What'll you do?

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.110
I'm going up.

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.330
How?

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.370
Shinonome-san,

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:24.330
I'll surpass you and move onwards.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.790
Great. Bring it.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:35.590
Hiyah!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.060
Even in a dream, that hurt!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.020
I see.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.470
Guess this really is a dream.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:45.120
There's no way you'd be 
this strong, Yuu-kun.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.470
A dream? Yes, it's a dream.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.900
So I really can go all-out!

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:52.860
Not enough!

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:58.770
You're good, but your movements 
don't match your build.

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:01.080
You're still pretty skilled,

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.910
but it's not enough 
against a genius like me.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:05.740
<i>He sees right through me.</i>

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:06.740
<i>But still...</i>

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.920
Genius!

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.380
Is infinite affirmation!

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:18.170
It's taking your incredible intuition 
that you can land a lucky blow,

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:22.220
then affirming it a thousand times over 
instead of ever denying it as impossible!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.940
So long as you can affirm that intuition,

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.450
you'll realize a thousand 
lucky blows and be awesome!

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:28.640
That is genius!

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:29.770
Technique is just a bonus!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.000
It's taking that moment of awesome,

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.950
that chance to be awesome,

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.450
and affirming, affirming, 
and affirming it some more!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.780
Don't think!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.060
Keep intuiting!

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.200
Keep affirming!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.660
Keep holding that conviction!

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:46.770
<i>Shinonome-san truly is incredible.</i>

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.400
<i>Though that's just him!</i>

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.650
<i>I think!</i>

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.310
<i>I keep thinking,</i>

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.130
<i>I keep questioning,</i>

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.810
<i>and I keep answering!</i>

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.200
Guess it's time to use it.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:07.850
Holding Domain: Babylon!

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.040
<i>His Holding Field thinned 
out and disappeared?</i>

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.830
<i>What is this sensation?</i>

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.170
<i>A punch?! He's fast!</i>

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.740
<i>No, actually...</i>

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.210
<i>I'm slow?!</i>

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.620
Hiyah!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.370
Wh-What's with that monstrous strength?!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.540
That's dangerous!

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.670
Well, where indeed?

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.130
Holding Domain: Babylon.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.740
By surrounding myself in a Holding Field

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.390
that's been thinned and spread 
into a low-density sphere,

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:38.020
I can simultaneously strengthen 
the acceleration of my own agility,

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:41.140
and hamper the movements of my opponents!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:42.800
How do I need to move?

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:44.190
How do I need to support it?

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:46.560
How do I need to interfere 
with my opponent's movements?

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:50.720
I can't use this ability if I stop 
thinking for even a second!

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:53.980
Even if you understood, I think 
you'd have difficulty breaking it.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.020
Hah, interesting!

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:58.140
Through wisdom, I gain courage!

00:18:58.140 --> 00:18:59.950
Now, shall we continue?

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.500
<i>He's fast on the exchange, 
in addition to that crazy strength.</i>

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.260
<i>If I get close to him, the timing 
of my grabs gets thrown off.</i>

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.330
<i>This is...</i>

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.920
You can't win.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.390
He who inherited the one that intuits.

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.350
He who admires the one with courage.

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:18.860
He who thinks.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.820
It's three against one.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:23.140
Now! I will...

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.050
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:26.890
...surpass you!

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:35.170
Dreams are crazy, man.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:38.780
I never imagined an invincible guy 
like me would lose to you, Yuu-kun.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:40.410
Dreams?

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:43.760
Well, since this is a dream, 
please be sure to remember it.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:47.700
Next time a golem comes and I'm in danger...

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.500
please don't save me.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.350
Of course I won't.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:54.580
I'm the one who wants saving.

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:58.050
I wouldn't risk my life 
to protect someone else.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.260
But you'll still save me anyway.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.050
Because you're a hero to the core.

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:03.710
Oh, wait.

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:07.260
If her student died, Hisame would cry.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.740
She'd cry if you died, too.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.930
Well, I'll be going now.

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.610
Oh, wait a second.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.940
Here. Congratulations.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.640
Why are you crying while smiling?

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.180
Oh, it's nothing.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:25.800
Farewell.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.840
Nice to meet you, Amamiya Yuuhi-kun.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.490
Uh, and you are?

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.700
Akitani Inatika.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:46.390
People call me "Master".

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:47.540
You're him?

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:50.030
I watched your fight just now.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:51.170
You're incredible.

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:51.910
Thanks.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:54.930
Um, Akitani-san, what...

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.600
time are you from right now?

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:00.070
I just finished writing my book.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:02.070
It's the night before I meet my fate.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:04.830
I read your book. It was interesting.

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:06.070
Thank you.

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:10.030
I didn't expect to hear an impression 
the moment I finished it.

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.050
Um,

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.500
are you here to stop me, too, Akitani-san?

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:18.070
No, Anima only called me here to watch.

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.320
Go on ahead.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:20.180
Okay.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:23.050
Also...

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:26.050
How are the children doing?

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:27.400
They're well.

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.050
They're very reliable.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.550
I see.

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:31.840
Oh, right.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:34.540
May I shake your hand, as well?

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:35.850
Oh, sure.

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:39.110
Farewell.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.780
<i>Man, this is a long staircase.</i>

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.980
Now you, Anima?

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:58.620
How did you get ahead of me 
when I climbed straight up?

00:21:58.620 --> 00:21:59.670
Don't worry about it.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.290
Well, still, thank you.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:03.860
For letting me see Shinonome-san.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:05.230
Huh? Anima?

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:09.530
Your reward for making it this far. Now go.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:11.250
H-Huh?

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:12.470
Hmm...

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:16.410
P-Princess...

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:19.400
Well, I'll pretend I didn't see that one.

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:20.900
Th-Thanks.

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:24.360
But don't forget, Yuu-kun,

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:26.450
you're mine.

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:28.010
Yes.

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:31.470
Go on. The goal's just ahead.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.920
Why?

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:46.720
Why... can I see it from here?

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:50.840
The Biscuit Hammer!

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:27.480
<b>Next Episode: 
Maimakterion and the Beast Knights</b>
